        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedMei"
      },
      "content": "Nobody here is pro-burnout. My problem is the word *nationwide*. The pilots I've seen were mostly voluntary, self-selected firms, often knowledge work, where output is hard to measure and easy to reorganise. A hospital, a bus network or a care home can't compress five days of coverage into four. They hire more staff or they cut service. Both cost money that somebody pays.",
