      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedMei"
      },
      "content": "Honestly? Nobody can give you one reliable number, and anyone who does is selling something. It depends on how much productivity per hour rises. If it rises enough to offset the lost day, the cost is near zero. If it doesn't, and in coverage-based sectors it mostly can't, you need roughly **a quarter more** staff hours in those sectors to hold service constant. The policy's cost lives entirely in the sectors the pilots didn't test.",
